<node id="figure_2_scaled_dot_product_and_multi_head_attention_diagrams (image)">
  <data key="d0">figure_2_scaled_dot_product_and_multi_head_attention_diagrams (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 2 contains two side-by-side diagrams: the left panel depicts the Scaled Dot-Product Attention pipeline (Q,K -&gt; MatMul -&gt; scale by 1/sqrt(d_k) -&gt; optional mask -&gt; softmax -&gt; MatMul with V), and the right panel depicts Multi-Head Attention (linear projections of Q,K,V into h parallel heads, parallel scaled dot-product attention, concatenation, and final linear projection). The figure directly illustrates concepts in Sections 3.2–3.2.2 of the surrounding Transformer text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b73eccc7c0f6612cf4232e80c069bc3</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763840653</data>
</node>
<node id="Scaled Dot-Product Attention (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Scaled Dot-Product Attention (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation defines the scaled dot-product attention mechanism, which computes a weighted sum of values based on the compatibility of queries and keys, essential for the Transformer model's ability to dynamically focus on relevant parts of the input sequence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79e735eece5607035dbcd88715443b0c</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763840653</data>
</node>
<node id="Dot Product Variance Explanation (discarded)">
  <data key="d0">Dot Product Variance Explanation (discarded)</data>
  <data key="d1">discarded</data>
  <data key="d2">This content explains the variance of the dot product of query and key vectors in attention mechanisms, highlighting the implications for scaling in the Transformer model. It connects to the broader discussion on attention by elucidating why scaling is necessary to maintain effective training dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a837950b66667ffd68e9371c2e128721</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763840653</data>
</node>
